      "text": "Day 23: Redux Thunk: \nIn this class I learnt redux thunk. Redux thunk is a outer action\nof redux that used for synk api with redux. I created 4 layer architecture\ninside src i created folders name is: app, features, routes, shared, and config.\nin features folder i created 4 another folder api, hooks, state, ui. We know\nthis 4 folder mean 4 layer architecture. inside ui i created another folder pages\nand component inside pages i created loginPage.jsx and registerPage.jsx. \nand wrote code of login and register page inside hooks folder i created authHook.jsx\nfile and inside file i wrote custom hook useAuth() insdie useAuth funciton\nI used useForm() hook for handle form data and loginForm or registerForm\nfunction, useNavigate() and then return { handleSubmit, errors, navigate, register,\nregisterForm, loginForm, showPassword, setShowPassword };  after that\nuse useAuth on loginPage and registerPage and handle login form there using\nthis custom hook. inside state I create authslice.jsx file and inside i create \nauthSlice using createSlice(). After I wrote name: auth, initialState: { user: null,\nisLoading: false, isAuthenticated: false }  after that I created reducers this is\n  reducers: {\n    addUser: (state, action) => {\n      state.user = action.payload;\n      state.isLoading = false;\n    },\n    removeUser: (state) => {\n      state.user = null;\n      state.isLoading = false;\n    },\n  },\n\nin config folder i created api instance using aixos.create and give dummyjson api\nimport axios from \"axios\";\n\nexport const api = axios.create({\n    baseURL: \"https://dummyjson.com\",\n    withCredentials: true\n})\n\nafter  in auth/state folder i create authAction.jsx and inside i created \nloginUserAction = createAsyncThunk() below is complete code\nexport const loginUserAction = createAsyncThunk(\n  \"auth/login\",\n  async (credentials, thunkApi) => {\n    try {\n      let res = await api.post(\"/auth/login\", credentials);\n      toast.success(\"User logged\");\n      localStorage.setItem(\"accessToken\", res.data.accessToken);\n      return res.data;\n    } catch (error) {\n      return thunkApi.rejectWithValue(\"login failed\");\n    }\n  },\n);\n\nfor hydration i saved accessToken inside localstore for accessing logged user after reload page.\n\nafter on auth/hooks folder inside loginform function there when user submit\nlogin form then there is data comming so inside loginform i used dispatch(loginUserAction(data))\ni pass login form data inside loginUserAction. and then on authslice file I wrote extraReducer. \ni see reduxthunk return three state pending, fulffiled and rejected. \nthen on authslice i used extraReducer for api action then inside one callback inside callback\nreceiver argument builder then builder.addCase below is complete code. \nextraReducers: (builder) => {\n    builder\n      .addCase(loginUserAction.pending, (state, action) => {\n        state.isLoading = true;\n      })\n      .addCase(loginUserAction.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n        state.user = action.payload;\n        state.isAutheticated = true;\n        state.isLoading = false;\n      })\n      .addCase(loginUserAction.rejected, (state, action) => {\n        state.isLoading = false;\n        toast.error(\"login failed\");\n      })\n}\n\n\non routing part I created data routing. \nconst AppRoutes = () => {\nconst dispatch = useDispatch();\n   useEffect(() => {\n    dispatch(hydrateUserAction())\n   }, [])\n\n    const router = createBrowserRouter([\n        {\n           path: \"/\",\n           element: <AuthProtected/>,\n           children: [\n            {\n                path: \"\", \n                element: <AuthLayout/>,\n                children: [\n                    {\n                        path: \"\", \n                        element: <LoginPage/>\n\n                    },\n                    {\n                        path: \"register\",\n                        element: <RegisterPage/>\n                    }\n                ]\n            }\n           ] \n        }, \n        {\n            path: \"/main\", \n            element: <MainProtected/>,\n            children: [\n                {\n                    path: \"\", \n                    element: <MainLayout/>, \n                    children: [\n                        {\n                            path: \"\", \n                            element: <HomePage/>\n                        }, \n                        {\n                            path: \"product\", \n                            element: <ProductPage/>\n                        }, \n                        {\n                            path: \"cart\", \n                            element: <CartPage/>\n                        },\n                        {\n                            path: \"order\", \n                            element: <OrderPage/>\n                        }, \n                        \n                    ]\n                }\n            ]\n        }\n    ])\n  return <RouterProvider router={router}/>\n}\n\nexport default AppRoutes;\n\n\ni prevent auth layout and mainlayout using protected route. \nwhen reload page then redux state data of user set nulll for that i used hydration \ninside state/authAction.jsx i do hydration using access token that saved during\nlogin. this is code of hydartion. \nexport const hydrateUserAction = createAsyncThunk(\n  \"auth/hydrate\",\n  async (_, thunkApi) => {\n    let token = localStorage.getItem(\"accessToken\");\n    try {\n      let res = await api.get(\"/auth/me\", {\n        headers: {\n          Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,\n        },\n      });\n      return res.data;\n    } catch (error) {\n      toast.error(\"Unauthorized user\");\n      return thunkApi.rejectWithValue(\"Hydration Failed\");\n    }\n  },\n);\n\n\nand i called hydrateUserAction function inside approutes using useEffect()\nafter that in auth/state/authslice.jsx inside i wrote three state inside \nextraReducer of hydrateUserAction. like this.\n\n .addCase(hydrateUserAction.pending, (state, action) => {\n        state.isLoading = true;\n      })\n      .addCase(hydrateUserAction.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n        state.user = action.payload;\n        state.isAutheticated = true;\n        state.isLoading = false;\n      })\n      .addCase(hydrateUserAction.rejected, (state, action) => {\n        state.isLoading = false;\n      });\n\n\nI used inbuild dummy json api for user login, userName: emilys password: emilyspass",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Day 23: Redux Thunk: \nIn this class I learnt redux thunk. Redux thunk is a outer action\nof redux that used for synk api with redux. I created 4 layer architecture\ninside src i created folders name is: app, features, routes, shared, and config.\nin features folder i created 4 another folder api, hooks, state, ui. We know\nthis 4 folder mean 4 layer architecture. inside ui i created another folder pages\nand component inside pages i created loginPage.jsx and registerPage.jsx. \nand wrote code of login and register page inside hooks folder i created authHook.jsx\nfile and inside file i wrote custom hook useAuth() insdie useAuth funciton\nI used useForm() hook for handle form data and loginForm or registerForm\nfunction, useNavigate() and then return { handleSubmit, errors, navigate, register,\nregisterForm, loginForm, showPassword, setShowPassword };  after that\nuse useAuth on loginPage and registerPage and handle login form there using\nthis custom hook. inside state I create authslice.jsx file and inside i create \nauthSlice using createSlice(). After I wrote name: auth, initialState: { user: null,\nisLoading: false, isAuthenticated: false }  after that I created reducers this is\n  reducers: {\n    addUser: (state, action) => {\n      state.user = action.payload;\n      state.isLoading = false;\n    },\n    removeUser: (state) => {\n      state.user = null;\n      state.isLoading = false;\n    },\n  },\n\nin config folder i created api instance using aixos.create and give dummyjson api\nimport axios from \"axios\";\n\nexport const api = axios.create({\n    baseURL: \"https://dummyjson.com\",\n    withCredentials: true\n})\n\nafter  in auth/state folder i create authAction.jsx and inside i created \nloginUserAction = createAsyncThunk() below is complete code\nexport const loginUserAction = createAsyncThunk(\n  \"auth/login\",\n  async (credentials, thunkApi) => {\n    try {\n      let res = await api.post(\"/auth/login\", credentials);\n      toast.success(\"User logged\");\n      localStorage.setItem(\"accessToken\", res.data.accessToken);\n      return res.data;\n    } catch (error) {\n      return thunkApi.rejectWithValue(\"login failed\");\n    }\n  },\n);\n\nfor hydration i saved accessToken inside localstore for accessing logged user after reload page.\n\nafter on auth/hooks folder inside loginform function there when user submit\nlogin form then there is data comming so inside loginform i used dispatch(loginUserAction(data))\ni pass login form data inside loginUserAction. and then on authslice file I wrote extraReducer. \ni see reduxthunk return three state pending, fulffiled and rejected. \nthen on authslice i used extraReducer for api action then inside one callback inside callback\nreceiver argument builder then builder.addCase below is complete code. \nextraReducers: (builder) => {\n    builder\n      .addCase(loginUserAction.pending, (state, action) => {\n        state.isLoading = true;\n      })\n      .addCase(loginUserAction.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n        state.user = action.payload;\n        state.isAutheticated = true;\n        state.isLoading = false;\n      })\n      .addCase(loginUserAction.rejected, (state, action) => {\n        state.isLoading = false;\n        toast.error(\"login failed\");\n      })\n}\n\n\non routing part I created data routing. \nconst AppRoutes = () => {\nconst dispatch = useDispatch();\n   useEffect(() => {\n    dispatch(hydrateUserAction())\n   }, [])\n\n    const router = createBrowserRouter([\n        {\n           path: \"/\",\n           element: <AuthProtected/>,\n           children: [\n            {\n                path: \"\", \n                element: <AuthLayout/>,\n                children: [\n                    {\n                        path: \"\", \n                        element: <LoginPage/>\n\n                    },\n                    {\n                        path: \"register\",\n                        element: <RegisterPage/>\n                    }\n                ]\n            }\n           ] \n        }, \n        {\n            path: \"/main\", \n            element: <MainProtected/>,\n            children: [\n                {\n                    path: \"\", \n                    element: <MainLayout/>, \n                    children: [\n                        {\n                            path: \"\", \n                            element: <HomePage/>\n                        }, \n                        {\n                            path: \"product\", \n                            element: <ProductPage/>\n                        }, \n                        {\n                            path: \"cart\", \n                            element: <CartPage/>\n                        },\n                        {\n                            path: \"order\", \n                            element: <OrderPage/>\n                        }, \n                        \n                    ]\n                }\n            ]\n        }\n    ])\n  return <RouterProvider router={router}/>\n}\n\nexport default AppRoutes;\n\n\ni prevent auth layout and mainlayout using protected route. \nwhen reload page then redux state data of user set nulll for that i used hydration \ninside state/authAction.jsx i do hydration using access token that saved during\nlogin. this is code of hydartion. \nexport const hydrateUserAction = createAsyncThunk(\n  \"auth/hydrate\",\n  async (_, thunkApi) => {\n    let token = localStorage.getItem(\"accessToken\");\n    try {\n      let res = await api.get(\"/auth/me\", {\n        headers: {\n          Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,\n        },\n      });\n      return res.data;\n    } catch (error) {\n      toast.error(\"Unauthorized user\");\n      return thunkApi.rejectWithValue(\"Hydration Failed\");\n    }\n  },\n);\n\n\nand i called hydrateUserAction function inside approutes using useEffect()\nafter that in auth/state/authslice.jsx inside i wrote three state inside \nextraReducer of hydrateUserAction. like this.\n\n .addCase(hydrateUserAction.pending, (state, action) => {\n        state.isLoading = true;\n      })\n      .addCase(hydrateUserAction.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n        state.user = action.payload;\n        state.isAutheticated = true;\n        state.isLoading = false;\n      })\n      .addCase(hydrateUserAction.rejected, (state, action) => {\n        state.isLoading = false;\n      });\n\n\nI used inbuild dummy json api for user login, userName: emilys password: emilyspass",
